    rulesSection5Title: '5. Requirements, safety and organization',
    rulesSection1Body: `<p>Ulak Tartysh sporting competitions are held by decision of the <strong>Ulak Tartysh public association</strong> and in coordination with the authorized government body for physical culture and sport.</p><h3>Main competition goals:</h3><ul><li>promote Ulak Tartysh;</li><li>develop national equestrian sports;</li><li>preserve nomadic cultural traditions;</li><li>improve athletes' skills;</li><li>strengthen sporting friendship and cooperation.</li></ul><p><em>The competition name, procedure, time and venue are defined by its regulations.</em></p>`,
    rulesSection2Body: `<p>The game is played on a <strong>specially prepared field</strong>.</p><h3>Required field elements:</h3><ul><li><strong>central line and central zone</strong> — the starting point;</li><li><strong>scoring zone (maara)</strong> — the scoring area;</li><li><strong>side and end boundaries</strong> of the field;</li><li><strong>safety zone</strong> for referees and technical staff.</li></ul><p><em>Field dimensions and the technical layout are defined by the regulations.</em></p>`,
    rulesSection3Body: `<h3>Teams and rosters</h3><ul><li><strong>6 starting players</strong> on the field;</li><li><strong>4 substitute players</strong>.</li></ul><h3>Game duration</h3><ul><li><strong>regular time:</strong> 15 minutes;</li><li><strong>extra period:</strong> 10 minutes;</li><li>if there is no winner, a 2×2 contest is held.</li></ul><h3>Main game object</h3><ul><li>weight: <strong>35–45 kg</strong>;</li><li>it must be suitable and safe for play.</li></ul>`,
    rulesSection4Body: `<h3>Starting the game</h3><ul><li>play starts from the lower area of the field;</li><li>the referee places the game object at the marked point;</li><li>after the whistle, players enter the contest simultaneously.</li></ul><h3>A score is disallowed if:</h3><ul><li>the game object is dropped;</li><li>the player falls before reaching the maara;</li><li>the object does not fully enter the scoring area;</li><li>the player leaves the field.</li></ul><h3>Stopping play</h3><p>The referee <strong>immediately stops the game</strong> when a dangerous situation arises.</p>`,
    rulesSection5Body: `<h3>Horse and participant requirements</h3><ul><li>horses must be healthy and properly prepared;</li><li>age requirements are set by the regulations;</li><li>horses without a veterinary inspection are not admitted.</li></ul><h3>Violations and penalties</h3><ul><li>a two-minute suspension for a minor violation;</li><li>full removal for a serious violation;</li><li>striking, grabbing, aggression and dangerous actions are prohibited.</li></ul><h3>Organization</h3><p>The organizer provides field preparation, medical and veterinary supervision, and safety instructions.</p>`,
